# Citation metadata for the software and accompanying article.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the article and, if you need to
  reference a specific version of the code, the software as well.
type: software

title: >-
  Code and data for "Temporal Supervision Horizon and Latent-Dynamics
  Recovery in SIR Universal Differential Equations"

abstract: >-
  Reproducible companion to the article: the SIR-UDE library in Julia, the
  runners for the eleven experiments, the result files behind every value
  cited in the manuscript, the scripts that generate the six figures, and
  four checkers that recompute each cited value from the delivered data
  and report whether it matches.

